2.2.1
SECURITY-RELEVANT. v2.2.0 stopped the hooks assuming `node` (`hooks/lib/json.sh` tries node, then python3, then jq; the three git gates fail CLOSED with none of them), added an optional `**Protected branches**:` field, and fixed the bootstrap path end to end — but it shipped that field as a live `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}` placeholder, and the resolver returned the literal as a branch NAME, so every consumer who accepted the template has had an UNPROTECTED trunk since. v2.2.1 is one posture applied in five places: a gate that cannot determine the answer must refuse, not permit. An unreplaced `{{...}}` now resolves as if the line were absent (`main master`), an empty value warns and does the same, and `none` stays the one deliberate opt-out; a parser that is on PATH but does not work (the Windows App-Installer `python3` stub) is probed and treated as absent instead of returning "" for every field; a payload that does not parse — malformed, truncated, empty stdin — blocks with its own message instead of exiting 0; `enforce-delegation.sh`'s one unanchored pattern no longer false-denies on a hook path appearing in DATA; and `scripts/test-hooks.sh` itself, whose `node -e` payload builders made it report 128 harness failures on a node-less host, is now printf + sed with no interpreter at all. Plus: `/sync-template` step 1b never collected `hooks/lib/json.sh` (seven hooks silently inactive after a compliant sync), step 3's `Bash(true)` smoke test could not tell a healthy gate from an inert one and is now a both-ways probe run from a script file, a mandatory pre-sync backup of the gitignored-but-manifest-tracked files (`CLAUDE.local.md` is unrecoverable — no history, no diff, no undo), a mandatory post-apply placeholder sweep, `template-sync-tools >= 0.2.0` stated, and the parser named on the report's `Gates:` line. Two consistency checks that existed but did not cover the case: every `hooks/lib/*` must be mirrored, and every shipped shell script must parse (one apostrophe inside a `node -e '…'` body disables the whole hook). 12 hook scripts + `hooks/lib/`, 8 skills; 259 consistency assertions, 299 hook fixtures.
